    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Form an equation and solve.\n\nOf the total amount of money in his wallet, a man gave one-third to his daughter and one-quarter to his son. After this he only had $\\$250$ left. How much was originally in his wallet?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$600$",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the original amount in dollars. His daughter receives $\\dfrac{x}{3}$ dollars and his son receives $\\dfrac{x}{4}$ dollars.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x-\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{x}{4}&=250\\\\12x-4x-3x&=3000\\\\5x&=3000\\\\x&=\\frac{3000}{5}\\\\x&=600\\end{align*}$$\n\nOriginally, his wallet contained $\\$600$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
